;; Eve's layers, derived from the tree (hosts.edn + the namespace
;; census on syntax/formalization-1, Nov 22 2026; corrected
;; 2026-11-23, see the :net note):
;;
;; :host-seam — the primitive namespaces ONLY adapters define
;; (eve.host, eve.codec, eve.slab-io, eve.crypto, ...): each host
;; supplies its own file for the same namespace. src/ (the core)
;; requires these namespaces but never defines them; adapter files
;; require core namespaces back (host impls build on core utils).
;; That mutual seam<->core reach is Eve's actual architecture: the
;; conditional guarantee is "if the adapter primitives satisfy the
;; contract, the core's guarantees hold" — so seam and core may
;; access each other, and both are closed to the apps.
;;
;; :core — every eve.* namespace defined under src/ (the CLJC core).
;;
;; :net — the network-atoms subsystem (the eve.net.* namespaces
;; defined under apps/network-atoms/src). CORRECTION (2026-11-23):
;; the first model put every eve.net.* name in :apps, which was
;; wrong twice over. (1) eve.net.bytes, eve.net.json and
;; eve.net.u64 are defined under src/ — they are core. (2) The
;; network-atoms namespaces are not a leaf application: the core's
;; own eve.thread.net (the thread layer's network rung) and
;; eve.keyring require eve.net.atom/platform/run/wire and
;; eve.net.crypto directly — network atoms are an Eve subsystem
;; the core builds on, so :net sits between :core and :apps:
;; core and apps may access it, it may access core and the seam.
;; The mis-model was invisible until the lint-depend leg was made
;; non-vacuous (it had analyzed zero namespaces since its first
;; run; see bb.edn). Whether eve.thread.net/eve.keyring should
;; instead move out of the core is an architecture question for
;; the Eve owners, recorded in the lane's RETRO.md — this config
;; models the tree as it stands.
;;
;; :apps — the application namespaces (eve.aegis.*). Nothing in
;; the core, the seam or the net layer may depend on an app; apps
;; may depend on everything below them.
;;
;; Layer order matters: clj-depend assigns a namespace to the
;; FIRST layer whose :defined-by matches, so :apps and :net are
;; listed before the :core catch-all.
;;
;; Namespaces outside eve.* (clojure.*, goog.*) are not layered.
{:layers
 {:apps {:defined-by "eve\\.aegis\\..*"
         :accessed-by-layers #{:apps}}
  :net {:defined-by "eve\\.net\\.(atom|blobs|broker|broker-disk|codec|crypto|gateway|graft|pages|platform|presign|run|snapshot|stand-in|store|wire)(\\..*)?"
        :accessed-by-layers #{:apps :net :core}}
  :host-seam {:defined-by "eve\\.(codec|core|crypto|crypto-bigint|data|deftype-proto\\.wasm|encoding|flat-io|gc|host|host-completion|host-init|host-prim|http|http-server|int32|journal-file|logical-protocol|process|process-slab|region|rrb-vector\\.macros|sab|slab-io|thread-host|typed-view|types|types-js|util|wasm-mem)"
              :accessed-by-layers #{:host-seam :core :apps :net}}
  :core {:defined-by "eve\\..*"
         :accessed-by-layers #{:host-seam :core :apps :net}}}}
